      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8b9fa81d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: just_waterin'_the_dirt; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a child watering a dog with a hose, with the text 'just waterin' the dirt' overlaid. The meme's intent is to mock or ridicule the child's action by implying the child is wasting water or being absurdly literal, as if watering the dirt is the only purpose. This is a harmless, lighthearted joke that relies on the absurdity of the situation rather than targeting any individual or group. It does not contain any abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynous, or propagandistic content. The humor stems from the juxtaposition of the child's innocent action with the sarcastic text, which highlights the silliness of the situation without any harmful intent toward any protected group.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_450aaba4"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
