      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "child is watering the dirt",
      "description": "The text 'just waterin' the dirt' is an analogical mapping that projects the child's action (watering the ground) onto the textual phrase 'the dirt'. The child is visually depicted holding a hose and spraying water onto the ground, which is the literal interpretation of 'watering the dirt'. The text sarcastically implies the child is wasting water or being absurdly literal, creating a humorous contrast between the visual action and the textual commentary.",
