      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the child watering the dirt",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the child (VisualMaterial entity) holding the hose and watering the ground, as the meme's humor relies on the viewer identifying with the child's literal interpretation of 'watering' — the child is watering the dirt, not the dog. The user sees themselves in the child's innocent, naive, or absurdly literal action, which is the core of the joke. The projection is onto the visual material of the child performing the action, not onto any explicit deictic pronoun.",
